183
00:17:38,656 --> 00:17:43,621
لَا يَنْفَعُوْ نَفْسٌ إِيْمَانُهَا لَمْ تَكًنْ أَمَنَتْ مِنْ قَبْلَ أَوْ كَسَبَتْ فِيْ إِيْمَانِهَا خَيْرًا

184
00:17:44,125 --> 00:17:50,430
Rasool Allah ﷺ says when Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال) comes out publicly with his invitation to falsehood

185
00:17:50,997 --> 00:17:52,272
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

186
00:17:52,975 --> 00:17:58,276
A person who doesn't already have Emaan(إيمان) will not be able to attain it then.

187
00:17:59,515 --> 00:18:07,647
If you're not prepared in advance you will not be able to prepare when he comes out.

188
00:18:08,694 --> 00:18:13,272
So, you have to have prior preparation to be saved from the Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال)

189
00:18:13,491 --> 00:18:19,678
because his Fitnah(فِتْنَه) is so great no one will be able to attain Emaan(إيمان) when he comes out.

190
00:18:21,730 --> 00:18:23,958
So, you can see the value of being ahead,

191
00:18:24,387 --> 00:18:25,991
being ahead in everything

192
00:18:26,217 --> 00:18:32,424
and I'm saying this because of our tendency to have procrastination, we delay things.

193
00:18:34,178 --> 00:18:35,939
Ibn Qayyim(إبن قيم) in fact he says;

194
00:18:36,610 --> 00:18:42,957
If one would go through the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an which narrate

195
00:18:43,766 --> 00:18:45,744
what the people of Hellfire are saying

196
00:18:46,172 --> 00:18:55,572
one would find that the majority of their complaints are?

197
00:18:56,007 --> 00:18:58,167
How come we delayed it?

198
00:18:58,857 --> 00:19:00,215
Why did we wait?

199
00:19:00,596 --> 00:19:02,445
Why did we procrastinate?

200
00:19:05,234 --> 00:19:07,910
رَبّ ارْجِعُونِ لَعَلِّي أَعْمَلُ صَالِحًا فِيمَا تَرَكْتُ ۚ

201
00:19:07,992 --> 00:19:10,558
O Allah Take me back, so that I can do good.

202
00:19:12,101 --> 00:19:16,945
In another Ayah(آية) it says: O Allah take me back to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), so that I can make Infaaq(إنفاق) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

203
00:19:17,217 --> 00:19:19,738
In another Ayah(آية) it says: O Allah take me back to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

204
00:19:19,919 --> 00:19:22,819
I will believe in you and in the messenger and on and on.

205
00:19:24,003 --> 00:19:26,903
They delayed it, until it was too late.

206
00:19:29,787 --> 00:19:32,564
Abu Obaidah As-Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) he came first,

207
00:19:32,795 --> 00:19:37,923
he was appointed even though he had less experience in war.

208
00:19:38,474 --> 00:19:40,926
He was a Tabaee(تابعي) and not a Sahabi(صحابي).

209
00:19:41,513 --> 00:19:44,855
So in terms of status is lower than the Sahabah(صحابه), the Sahabah(صحابه) are higher

210
00:19:45,392 --> 00:19:48,567
But because he came first, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) appointed him.

211
00:19:51,024 --> 00:19:55,619
Sulait(سُلَيت) who is from Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار).

212
00:19:56,994 --> 00:19:59,773
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I would have appointed him

213
00:20:02,932 --> 00:20:07,156
but this Ansari(أنصاري) was in a rush.

214
00:20:08,855 --> 00:20:16,292
He wasn't a person who takes issues calmly, he rushes into things.

215
00:20:16,433 --> 00:20:19,506
He is very bold and aggressive and strong.

216
00:20:20,506 --> 00:20:24,803
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) didn't mind the person having such characteristics

217
00:20:25,170 --> 00:20:28,107
but he did not want such a person to lead an army.

218
00:20:30,143 --> 00:20:36,482
So, Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه told Abu Obaidah Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي), he said:

219
00:20:37,049 --> 00:20:41,284
إِسْمِعْ لِأَصْحَابِ رَسُوْلِ الله وَشِّرِكْهُمْ فِى الّأَمْر

220
00:20:41,963 --> 00:20:46,908
Listen to the advice of the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and

221
00:20:47,349 --> 00:20:50,896
take Shura(شورى) from them, take their advice.

222
00:20:52,373 --> 00:20:54,403
وَلَا تَجْتَعِدْ مُسْرِعًا

223
00:20:54,856 --> 00:21:01,635
بَلِتَّعِدْفَإِنَّهَا الّحَرْبَ لَا يُصْلِحُوْهَا إِلَّا رَجُلٌ مَقِيْسَ أَلَّذِيْ يَعْرِفُ الّفُرْسَا

224
00:21:02,679 --> 00:21:13,042
And do not be in a hurry and take it easy and slow down because this is war

225
00:21:13,574 --> 00:21:20,926
and only a man whose unrushed is appropriate to lead in a battle.

226
00:21:21,550 --> 00:21:24,763
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying that when it comes to war,

227
00:21:26,488 --> 00:21:33,238
the person who is leading the army needs to be a person who is unrushed, not in a hurry,

228
00:21:33,850 --> 00:21:41,687
who deliberates and looks at things from every and each angle and doesn't rush into affairs.

229
00:21:41,726 --> 00:21:42,335
Why?

230
00:21:42,430 --> 00:21:46,654
Because the lives of the Muslims are under your hands.

231
00:21:48,547 --> 00:21:49,547
And he said;

232
00:21:49,760 --> 00:21:52,972
وَلَا يَمْنَعَنِيْ أَنْ أَأُمِّرْ صُلَيْتًّا إِلَّا سّْرَتَه’ الّحَرْبَ

233
00:21:52,996 --> 00:21:57,015
The only reason why I'm not pointing Sulait(سُلَيت) is because he rushes things

234
00:21:58,851 --> 00:21:59,928
and Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

235
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,527
"أَلْأَجَلَ مِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ"

236
00:22:03,003 --> 00:22:06,038
Hastening things is from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ)

237
00:22:07,202 --> 00:22:12,077
because when you do things in a rush, you're prone to make mistakes.

238
00:22:13,382 --> 00:22:16,470
And Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) uses these mistakes against you.

239
00:22:19,790 --> 00:22:25,157
Now, this doesn't mean that you should be so slow that you don't get anything done.

240
00:22:26,165 --> 00:22:27,704
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he says;

241
00:22:28,124 --> 00:22:29,604
"وَيَتَحَيَّرُالّفُرْسَا"

242
00:22:30,426 --> 00:22:34,825
A man who's unrushed but takes advantage of opportunities.

243
00:22:36,364 --> 00:22:42,508
So, when you see an opportunity you take it you go for it, you don't wait

244
00:22:42,788 --> 00:22:46,319
and think about it and no you go and take advantage of it.

245
00:22:48,124 --> 00:22:54,738
Abu Obaidah Assaqafi رضي الله عنه leads this army of about 7000

246
00:22:56,488 --> 00:23:01,872
in the end he was able to mobilize the force of 10,000 before he met with the enemy

247
00:23:02,319 --> 00:23:04,492
and he travelled towards Al-Iraq.

248
00:23:08,796 --> 00:23:15,940
They reached to a river and the enemy is across the river, the other side

249
00:23:18,289 --> 00:23:20,869
and now they're prepared to fight.

250
00:23:21,797 --> 00:23:28,026
So the enemy's General, he told Abu Obaidah Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي),

251
00:23:28,368 --> 00:23:30,614
Are you going to cross to us?

252
00:23:31,662 --> 00:23:34,295
Or shall we cross over to you?

253
00:23:35,650 --> 00:23:39,136
The Muslims told Abu Obaid(أبوعبيد); Let them cross over to us.

254
00:23:39,819 --> 00:23:41,290
Abu Obaid(أبوعبيد) Said: No.

255
00:23:41,821 --> 00:23:44,176
إِنَّهُمْ لَيْسُ بِأَجْرَأَلّْمَوْتِ مِنَّا

256
00:23:46,149 --> 00:23:50,255
They are not more willing to die than we are.

257
00:23:50,533 --> 00:23:52,653
So, let's cross over to them.

258
00:23:54,175 --> 00:24:01,386
So, they crossed over this bridge and they reached to the other side of the river.

259
00:24:03,055 --> 00:24:07,367
But the problem is that they were in a very narrow area,

260
00:24:08,180 --> 00:24:11,730
the enemy did not give them sufficient room to move in.

261
00:24:12,549 --> 00:24:19,150
So, they were constrained, they were constricted and the battle started

262
00:24:21,025 --> 00:24:26,075
and the Persians employed a weapon, which was unfamiliar to the Arabs

263
00:24:27,356 --> 00:24:29,254
and that was the elephant.

264
00:24:30,559 --> 00:24:36,047
They used elephants to fight and these were well trained elephants.

265
00:24:38,164 --> 00:24:41,019
And you would have soldiers on top of these elephants

266
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:47,056
and they attached to the elephants bells

267
00:24:48,158 --> 00:24:51,728
that would make a very raging, ringing sound very loud

268
00:24:52,631 --> 00:24:55,431
and that spooked the horses.

269
00:24:56,608 --> 00:25:01,013
So, now the entire Muslim cavalry was neutralized,

270
00:25:04,075 --> 00:25:10,212
none of the horses was willing to attack because of this violent sound

271
00:25:10,263 --> 00:25:13,035
that they would hear coming from the elephants.

272
00:25:15,859 --> 00:25:19,698
So, you have the entire cavalry is now out of the battle.

273
00:25:21,133 --> 00:25:23,902
So, now only the Muslim infantry was involved,

274
00:25:25,016 --> 00:25:27,607
and the archers were hitting them from every direction.

275
00:25:27,966 --> 00:25:29,466
So, the Muslims were dropping.

276
00:25:31,861 --> 00:25:36,571
Abu Obaidah Assaqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) realize the difficulty of the situation.

277
00:25:37,247 --> 00:25:41,719
He said: We have to get rid of these elephants, otherwise, we'll be massacred

278
00:25:43,255 --> 00:25:51,571
our horses are not able to attack and we are on foot and we are facing the elephants.

279
00:25:51,596 --> 00:25:55,200
We are facing their cavalry and we are facing their foot soldiers.

280
00:25:59,029 --> 00:26:02,916
And the Muslim cavalry was the most important portion of the army.

281
00:26:04,529 --> 00:26:06,511
That's where the Fursaan(فرسان) are, the fighters are.

282
00:26:08,303 --> 00:26:10,951
So, Abu Obaidah Assaqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) gave his commands;

283
00:26:11,284 --> 00:26:16,657
Go and cut the ropes that are holding the saddles,

284
00:26:17,316 --> 00:26:20,135
because every elephant has a saddle on top of it,

285
00:26:20,385 --> 00:26:22,857
and there are group of soldiers on top of the elephant.

286
00:26:22,913 --> 00:26:28,581
 So, Abu Obaidah Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) thought, if we're able to bring down those soldiers from on top of the elephants,

287
00:26:28,940 --> 00:26:31,900
then the elephants would be without anyone to lead them.

288
00:26:32,781 --> 00:26:39,144
So, they went around cutting the saddles, until they drop them from on top of the elephants.

289
00:26:39,453 --> 00:26:43,148
But that did not solve the problem because these were trained elephants,

290
00:26:43,687 --> 00:26:46,885
and they were just stumbling across the army,

291
00:26:47,127 --> 00:26:49,988
stepping over Muslims and crushing them under their feet.

292
00:26:51,526 --> 00:26:54,973
Abu Obaidah Assaqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) said: We must then kill these elephants.

293
00:26:54,998 --> 00:26:56,512
But these are huge animals.

294
00:26:56,684 --> 00:26:59,766
How can you kill the elephant with the sword or a spear or an arrow?

295
00:27:01,621 --> 00:27:04,206
Abu Obaidah Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) asked: How can we get rid of them?

296
00:27:04,963 --> 00:27:12,307
They said: Cut the trunk, if you cut the trunk of the elephant, it would die.

297
00:27:12,424 --> 00:27:15,269
That's what they, that's the advice he was given.

298
00:27:17,148 --> 00:27:21,779
Abu Obaidah Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) himself, even though he's the leader of the army,

299
00:27:21,804 --> 00:27:27,993
he went ahead in order to cut off the trunk of this elephant.

300
00:27:29,074 --> 00:27:34,023
But when he attempted to reach to the trunk of the elephant,

301
00:27:34,364 --> 00:27:41,373
the elephant struck Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيد) with his foot and stepped over Abu Obaid(ابوعبيد) and crushed him,

302
00:27:42,428 --> 00:27:46,936
Abu Obaidah Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي), the Ameer(أمير) of the Muslim army died, Shaheed(شهيد).

303
00:27:48,154 --> 00:27:53,185
His brother took over and he went to attack the same elephant, and was again crushed.

304
00:27:54,122 --> 00:27:57,812
So, his brother, Al-Hakam Bin Masood(ألحكم بن مسعود) died.

305
00:28:00,966 --> 00:28:02,046
They carried on.

306
00:28:02,317 --> 00:28:08,778
Now, Abu Obaid(ابوعبيد) appointed seven of his family members as Umaraa(أمرآء) in case he dies.

307
00:28:09,153 --> 00:28:13,455
So, if he died, it's his brother and his brother died, then it's his son,

308
00:28:13,748 --> 00:28:21,186
if his son dies, then his other son anyway, seven of his family members to assume leadership in case he dies.

309
00:28:22,164 --> 00:28:28,609
All of the seven were killed, all of the seven from the same family of Abu Obaidah Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) were killed.

310
00:28:30,297 --> 00:28:34,864
At the end of the day Al-Musanna Bin Harisa Shaibaani(ألْمثنى بن حارثه ألشيباني),

311
00:28:35,270 --> 00:28:42,469
he assumed the Imara(عمارة) of the army and he asked the Muslims to retreat.

312
00:28:44,166 --> 00:28:50,829
Al-Musanna(ألمثنى) saw that in this situation, we have a justified reason for retreating

313
00:28:51,165 --> 00:28:55,313
we should not carry on fighting, so he asked the Muslims to retreat.

314
00:28:57,106 --> 00:28:59,307
So, the Muslims are going on this bridge,

315
00:29:01,394 --> 00:29:11,863
Abdullah bin Marsad As-Saqqafi(عبدالله بن مرصد الثقفي) he went to the bridge and he told the Muslims;

316
00:29:12,274 --> 00:29:17,760
We should die just like our leaders died, do not retreat.

317
00:29:18,909 --> 00:29:22,041
Maybe this was before Musanna(مثنى) gave his instructions but anyway,

318
00:29:22,066 --> 00:29:26,102
the Muslims were already retreating even before the instructions of Al-Musanna(ألمثنى).

319
00:29:26,790 --> 00:29:32,384
So, the Muslims were retreating and Abdullah Bin Marsad(عبدالله بن مرصد) went to the bridge

320
00:29:33,384 --> 00:29:40,438
and he was telling the Muslims do not retreat, we should fight and die like our leaders did.

321
00:29:41,491 --> 00:29:42,659
And what did he do?

322
00:29:43,186 --> 00:29:45,606
He cut the bridge.

323
00:29:47,083 --> 00:29:51,687
You know this was a rope bridge, so he cut it down

324
00:29:54,849 --> 00:29:56,491
he was brought to Al-Musanna(ألمثنى).

325
00:29:57,643 --> 00:30:00,597
Al-Musanna(ألمثنى) beaten him so badly and, he said;

326
00:30:00,672 --> 00:30:02,224
Why did you do that?

327
00:30:03,438 --> 00:30:08,443
Abdullah(عبدالله) said: I did so that they would carry on fighting.

328
00:30:09,888 --> 00:30:14,792
Al-Musanna Bin Harisa(ألمثنى بن حارثه) gave his instructions that the bridge should be tied again.

329
00:30:15,306 --> 00:30:21,466
And that the Muslims should retreat, he saw it as a fatal thing to do.

330
00:30:21,822 --> 00:30:24,981
We have no chance of winning this battle, we need to retreat

331
00:30:25,661 --> 00:30:29,316
the elephants were just massacring the Muslims.

332
00:30:29,777 --> 00:30:32,877
The cavalry was not involved in the fighting,

333
00:30:33,153 --> 00:30:37,015
he asked the Muslims to retreat and Al-Musanna(ألمثنى) told them;

334
00:30:37,818 --> 00:30:43,521
"I want you to retreat peacefully and I am going to protect you

335
00:30:43,791 --> 00:30:48,602
until you all reach to the other side and then I will cross over."

336
00:30:50,334 --> 00:30:55,300
So, Al-Musanna Bin Harisa(ألمثنى بن حارثه), he is the leader but he wants to ensure that he leaves the last.

337
00:30:57,201 --> 00:31:00,251
By the way, Abdullah Bin Marsad(عبدالله بن مرصد) when it cut down the bridge, what happened is

338
00:31:00,545 --> 00:31:03,849
there are many Muslims already on their way to crossing the bridge.

339
00:31:04,107 --> 00:31:05,758
So, they were very close to the river

340
00:31:06,059 --> 00:31:11,750
and because the army of the enemy was so close to them and was pushing them many of them fell in the river and died,

341
00:31:12,765 --> 00:31:14,225
they drowned in the river.

342
00:31:17,988 --> 00:31:20,588
4000 Muslims were killed in that battle

343
00:31:21,221 --> 00:31:24,062
it's called the Battle of the bridge, 4000 many of them were Sahabah(صحابه).

344
00:31:24,346 --> 00:31:26,897
Now, when you say 4000, in those days that's a very high number.

345
00:31:29,338 --> 00:31:33,141
6000 Persians were killed.

346
00:31:37,989 --> 00:31:43,548
Musanna Bin Harisa(ألمثنى بن حارثه) retreated with the army and he went back to Madina.

347
00:31:45,306 --> 00:31:48,263
FEW THINGS RELATING TO THIS BATTLE, THE BATTLE OF AL-JISR(ألجسر)

348
00:31:49,259 --> 00:31:54,162
Number one; The wife of Abu Obaidah As-Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي), her name is Daoma(دومه)

349
00:31:54,187 --> 00:31:55,535
she saw a dream.

350
00:31:56,755 --> 00:32:03,887
She saw someone come from the heavens with a vessel in his hand

351
00:32:05,301 --> 00:32:08,758
and her husband Abu Obaid(ابوعبيد) came to drink from that vessel

352
00:32:09,770 --> 00:32:12,510
and then his son came to drink and his brother came to drink

353
00:32:12,942 --> 00:32:17,055
and she mentioned, the names of seven of his relatives.

354
00:32:19,211 --> 00:32:23,455
Abu Obaid As-Saqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) said: This indicates Shahadah(شهادة)

355
00:32:24,446 --> 00:32:26,883
the interpretation of this dream is Shahadah(شهادة).

356
00:32:29,782 --> 00:32:33,848
And that's why, he appointed these seven men to lead the army after him.

357
00:32:36,947 --> 00:32:41,053
Because he felt that these would die as Shuhada(شهداء).

358
00:32:41,627 --> 00:32:49,440
So, when he appointed them as leaders it's not as an honoring or a special status

359
00:32:49,495 --> 00:32:52,358
it is to put them in the front line, in the line of fire.

360
00:32:53,801 --> 00:32:56,068
To put them in the most risky post

361
00:32:57,260 --> 00:33:00,625
and his interpretation was true all of them died as a Shaheed(شهيد).

362
00:33:02,666 --> 00:33:07,861
When it comes to dreams brothers and sisters dreams are not interpreted equally

363
00:33:07,886 --> 00:33:11,403
so for example here, this means Shahadah(شهادة) that's not the only way

364
00:33:12,518 --> 00:33:14,508
Shahadah(شهادة) presents itself in a dream.

365
00:33:15,407 --> 00:33:19,688
With Tufail Bin Amr(طفيل بن عمرو) for example he saw that birds were eating from his head

366
00:33:21,025 --> 00:33:26,267
and that he was swallowed into a womb of a woman.

367
00:33:27,404 --> 00:33:33,080
He said: The interpretation of this dream is that my head will be chopped off

368
00:33:33,252 --> 00:33:34,463
and I will die as a Shaheed(شهيد)

369
00:33:35,400 --> 00:33:41,896
and the womb swallowing him is the earth swallowing his body, in his grave.

370
00:33:42,880 --> 00:33:44,131
So, that was Shahadah(شهادة).

371
00:33:44,607 --> 00:33:46,341
The way some people see Shahadah(شهادة) is

372
00:33:46,888 --> 00:33:51,910
they see themselves talking to Al-Hoor Ul Ain(حورالعين) before they die.

373
00:33:54,052 --> 00:33:56,714
With some, for example with Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان),

374
00:33:58,021 --> 00:34:00,552
Rasool Allah ﷺ came to him and his dream and he said;

375
00:34:01,201 --> 00:34:03,154
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was fasting that day.

376
00:34:03,443 --> 00:34:07,325
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ came to him in his dream and said: You're going to have Aftar(أفطار) with me

377
00:34:08,648 --> 00:34:10,132
and he died that day.

378
00:34:11,785 --> 00:34:14,357
So, Shahadah(شهادة) can come in different forms.

379
00:34:15,437 --> 00:34:22,633
So, the interpretation of dreams is more of  a gift from Allah than it is a science.

380
00:34:27,075 --> 00:34:32,669
We can also see that dreams played an important role in their lives.

381
00:34:32,693 --> 00:34:35,192
I mean, they would see dreams, they would interpret the dreams

382
00:34:35,485 --> 00:34:38,086
because this is the only thing remaining from Prophet hood.

383
00:34:38,438 --> 00:34:41,658
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: That all of the Prophethood will end with him

384
00:34:42,768 --> 00:34:44,692
and the only thing that will remain is,

385
00:34:44,717 --> 00:34:47,665
أَلرُّوْيَهْ أَلصَّادِقَهْ يَرَاهَلْ عَبْدَ الْمُؤمِنَ

386
00:34:48,021 --> 00:34:50,568
Is the true dream that a believer would see.

387
00:34:51,459 --> 00:34:58,576
So, this is the only form of revelation or inspiration that remains.

388
00:34:59,403 --> 00:35:03,515
Jibril عليه السّلام will never come down and deliver revelation to anyone.

389
00:35:05,332 --> 00:35:15,502
So, the only way in which we receive some of the ilm(علم) of the unseen is through dreams

390
00:35:15,564 --> 00:35:21,207
that are seen by Al-Momineen(ألمؤمنين) and these are Bisharat(بشارات).

391
00:35:21,232 --> 00:35:26,091
I think we talked earlier that there is no Halal(حلال) and Haram(حرام) that comes through a dream.

392
00:35:26,504 --> 00:35:30,742
The dream is only a Bishara(بشارة) it's good news, it's an indication of what will happen

393
00:35:31,445 --> 00:35:37,047
you cannot take a dream and use it to drive Ahkam(أحكام).

394
00:35:37,789 --> 00:35:39,897
The Ahkam(أحكام) are in Qur'an, and Sunnah(سنة).

395
00:35:43,051 --> 00:35:45,592
Number two, there were two mistakes committed,

396
00:35:47,448 --> 00:35:55,763
Number one: Abu Obaidah Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) not listening to the advice of his generals.

397
00:35:55,788 --> 00:35:59,837
When they said: Do not cross over to them, let them cross over to us.

398
00:36:01,189 --> 00:36:04,309
Abu Obaidah Saqqafi(أبوعبيد ألثقفي) was eager to go and fight,

399
00:36:05,587 --> 00:36:09,505
he saw it as an inappropriate for them to come to us

400
00:36:09,545 --> 00:36:11,616
because we want to die more than them

401
00:36:13,883 --> 00:36:18,981
and the Persians surrounded them because of that.

402
00:36:19,907 --> 00:36:24,762
Number two: The second mistake was Abdullah Bin Marsad(عبدالله بن مرصد), cutting the bridge

403
00:36:28,302 --> 00:36:31,593
and that was putting the Muslims in a very difficult situation.

404
00:36:31,618 --> 00:36:35,038
They're unable to retreat and it was too difficult for them to fight

405
00:36:35,063 --> 00:36:39,519
because the ranks were not organized and because of the elephants.

406
00:36:41,140 --> 00:36:53,100
So, bravery is good it's encouraged virtue, however, too much of that turns into recklessness.

407
00:36:55,979 --> 00:36:59,967
In fact, sometimes a person could be reckless even if they're a coward.

408
00:37:04,416 --> 00:37:09,594
A Muslim is supposed to have courage but they're not supposed to be reckless.

409
00:37:10,708 --> 00:37:17,223
A Muslim is supposed to think out things approach affairs with wisdom

410
00:37:17,802 --> 00:37:23,954
and not rush into anything because again, being in a hurry is from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ).

411
00:37:24,153 --> 00:37:25,723
ألعجل من الشّيطان

412
00:37:27,809 --> 00:37:28,655
Number three;

413
00:37:29,368 --> 00:37:32,504
"وَمَنْ يَتَّقِلَ الله يَجْعَلْ لَه’ مَخْرَجَا "

414
00:37:33,270 --> 00:37:36,875
The ones who have Taqwa(تقوى) in Allah, Allah will provide a way out for them.

415
00:37:38,020 --> 00:37:40,098
The Muslims were in a very, very difficult situation.

416
00:37:40,123 --> 00:37:42,573
Yes they retreated but they were still in the land of the enemy

417
00:37:43,596 --> 00:37:49,180
and the enemy could take advantage of that and just wipe them out, massacre them all,

418
00:37:50,791 --> 00:37:55,551
because 4000 Muslims were killed you only had a few thousand left

419
00:37:56,285 --> 00:38:02,508
and the enemy was 10s of thousands, they could recruit more.

420
00:38:03,926 --> 00:38:13,676
But Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, when He wants to save His followers

421
00:38:15,425 --> 00:38:24,323
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ creates the circumstances that facilitate saving them.

422
00:38:26,180 --> 00:38:29,561
You see Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is the One, Who controls everything in the heavens and earth.

423
00:38:30,863 --> 00:38:34,553
You might look at it in the beginning and say if you're looking at it

424
00:38:34,643 --> 00:38:37,741
from an approach of one plus one equals two logically.

425
00:38:39,573 --> 00:38:42,667
It's impossible the Muslims will be wiped out.

426
00:38:43,912 --> 00:38:47,019
But keep in mind that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has promised that

427
00:38:47,044 --> 00:38:49,532
He would give assistance and help to Muttaqeen(ألمتقين).

428
00:38:51,162 --> 00:38:53,137
Yes, the Muslims have lost in this battle.

429
00:38:53,232 --> 00:38:58,613
They couldn't find the cure for the elephants issue

430
00:38:59,282 --> 00:39:08,877
but Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ created for them a climate that made it impossible on the Persians

431
00:39:09,209 --> 00:39:15,932
to look at the Islamic invasion of their land,

432
00:39:16,772 --> 00:39:21,414
and that is a dispute that broke out between Rustum(رستم) and Feroze(فيروز).

433
00:39:22,758 --> 00:39:28,613
Rustum(رستم) and Feroze(فيروز), were the highest two military leaders in Persia.

434
00:39:30,455 --> 00:39:34,418
A war or a fight, a dispute broke out between the two of them

435
00:39:36,346 --> 00:39:41,783
and that preoccupied them from looking into the Muslim army.

436
00:39:42,698 --> 00:39:47,498
So, even though the Muslim army was weak and was battered in that war,

437
00:39:48,073 --> 00:39:53,176
many of them are injured, they lost some of their best fighters but nobody attack them.

438
00:39:54,864 --> 00:39:57,408
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ saved them through this dispute.

439
00:39:58,903 --> 00:40:03,681
Just like a Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has prepared the grounds for the Hijrah(هجرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

440
00:40:04,681 --> 00:40:07,852
Right before Muhammad ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina,

441
00:40:09,064 --> 00:40:12,173
one of the worst battles between Al-Aus(ألأوس) and Al-Khazraj(ألخزرج) occurred

442
00:40:12,198 --> 00:40:13,339
and it was called the Youm-Ul-Buaas(أليوم بعاث).

443
00:40:15,031 --> 00:40:23,325
Ayesha رضي الله عنها said: Yaoum Buaas(أليوم بعاث) was a day of preparation for the Hijrah(هجرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

444
00:40:23,571 --> 00:40:28,673
because that is when the majority of the leaders of both camps were killed.

445
00:40:30,085 --> 00:40:32,287
So, the people were left without leaders

446
00:40:33,469 --> 00:40:41,452
and that enhanced their willingness to bring in a leader from outside - Muhammad ﷺ.

447
00:40:43,193 --> 00:40:46,105
If the people of Madina were living in a peaceful state,

448
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:50,921
they wouldn't have wanted to bring in somebody from outside to lead them.

449
00:40:51,781 --> 00:40:56,916
Why would anyone want to bring a leader, a foreign leader from outside

450
00:40:56,941 --> 00:40:59,971
and appoint him over them if everything is going on alright?

451
00:41:01,033 --> 00:41:05,546
But because they have been in this cycle of violence for a very long time

452
00:41:05,936 --> 00:41:09,747
Al-Aus(ألأوس) Wal-Khazraj(وألخزرج) at each other's necks for years and years

453
00:41:10,117 --> 00:41:13,913
because of the Battle of Buaas(بعاث) many of the leaders were killed.

454
00:41:14,374 --> 00:41:20,931
When they went to Muhammad ﷺ they said: Maybe Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will unify us

455
00:41:21,158 --> 00:41:25,000
and end the bloodshed that is happening among us, through you.

456
00:41:27,496 --> 00:41:31,648
So, that war of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة) that was going on between Al-Aus(ألأوس) Wal-Khazraj(وألخزرج)

457
00:41:32,028 --> 00:41:34,910
was a preparation for the Hijrah(هجرة) of Muhammad ﷺ.

458
00:41:35,770 --> 00:41:37,627
It was also another preparation

459
00:41:37,898 --> 00:41:47,184
because it made the men of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) the most ideal group to given nusra(نصرة) to Muhammad ﷺ.

460
00:41:49,300 --> 00:41:51,479
They were seasoned fighters, what they would do?

461
00:41:51,504 --> 00:41:57,247
Is wake up in the morning go and fight until night time and they would go back to bed, on a daily basis.

462
00:41:58,190 --> 00:42:02,500
The training was part of their life the fighting was part of their life.

463
00:42:03,182 --> 00:42:08,006
It was a prepared and ready army for Rasool Allah ﷺ, to take over.

464
00:42:09,147 --> 00:42:12,135
It was an honor that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has preserved for them,

465
00:42:12,632 --> 00:42:14,555
even though it happened through hardship.

466
00:42:15,661 --> 00:42:17,279
They suffered for years and years

467
00:42:17,732 --> 00:42:20,848
but that was a preparation for them to be the Ansaar(ألأنصار) of this religion.

468
00:42:21,116 --> 00:42:23,087
The ones who would give this religion a victory.

469
00:42:24,834 --> 00:42:31,459
Therefore, the Muslim should never give up, the Muslim should never fear the creation

470
00:42:32,287 --> 00:42:37,656
and say that the creation is stronger than me, is more better equipment than me,

471
00:42:37,898 --> 00:42:44,589
has more technology than me, I have no hope that's not how you should look at it,

472
00:42:45,207 --> 00:42:46,847
the way you should look at it is.

473
00:42:47,192 --> 00:42:49,688
If I have Taqwa(تقوى) Allah will give me victory

474
00:42:49,782 --> 00:42:51,450
no matter how strong the enemy is.!

475
00:42:51,795 --> 00:42:56,811
If I  don't have Taqwa(تقوى) Allah will humiliate me, no matter how weak my enemy is.

476
00:42:59,179 --> 00:43:01,113
It all goes back to Taqwa(تقوى).

477
00:43:07,473 --> 00:43:14,472
And in the future when Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will see that this Ummah(امة) deserves victory,

478
00:43:16,228 --> 00:43:21,178
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will prepare the circumstances that will facilitate that,

479
00:43:21,876 --> 00:43:29,210
No matter how wide the gap in technology is, no matter how wide the financial gap is,

480
00:43:30,519 --> 00:43:32,790
all of these issues are irrelevant,

481
00:43:33,675 --> 00:43:37,895
when it comes to the issue of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ giving victory to the ones who He loves.

482
00:43:40,047 --> 00:43:44,309
There is no way to compare between the strength of Musa عليه السّلام and Firaun(فرعون), no way.

483
00:43:44,930 --> 00:43:50,891
What are you going to compare Musa alone, عليه السّلام, against Firaun(فرعون).

484
00:43:51,215 --> 00:43:53,206
أَلَّذِيْ تَجْرِى لّْأَنْهَارُ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا

485
00:43:53,231 --> 00:43:55,626
Firaun(فرعون) says; Rivers are flowing under me.

486
00:43:57,302 --> 00:44:06,405
He was the superpower of the Earth at that time, he had the most powerful army in the world,

487
00:44:06,710 --> 00:44:13,589
he had all of the wealth you could ask for, he had the powerful security force, he had it all,

488
00:44:14,417 --> 00:44:20,242
but Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ made him commit mistakes that ended with his demise.

489
00:44:21,160 --> 00:44:27,763
Even though Firaun(فرعون) was intelligent leader, he was a wise man, with very strong abilities.

490
00:44:28,584 --> 00:44:31,236
He had the powerful army, he had the resources,

491
00:44:33,366 --> 00:44:38,978
he had the advisors to tell him how to plan and how to approach the problem of Musa(موسى) and Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل).

492
00:44:39,587 --> 00:44:42,159
And on the other hand, you had Musa(موسى) and Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل) are

493
00:44:42,446 --> 00:44:45,996
without any arms without any wealth, they were slaves, they were weak.

494
00:44:48,011 --> 00:44:54,430
But Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ made firaoun(فرعون), commit mistakes and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ guided Musa(موسى).

495
00:44:54,510 --> 00:44:55,682
 Musa عليه السّلام said;

496
00:44:55,707 --> 00:44:57,642
كَلَّا ۖ إِنَّ مَعِيَ رَبِّي سَيَهْدِينِ

497
00:44:58,255 --> 00:45:03,364
When Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل) said: O Musa(موسى) give up that's it, they're gonna kill us

498
00:45:03,389 --> 00:45:07,313
we have no chance, sea is in front of us and Firaun(فرعون) is behind us. What  can we do?

499
00:45:07,470 --> 00:45:11,923
We are without any weapons you promised us and you lied.

500
00:45:13,767 --> 00:45:16,107
You said, that Allah is going to save us and here we are,

501
00:45:16,732 --> 00:45:20,412
the sea in front of us, Firaun(فرعون) behind us, you tricked us, you fooled us.

502
00:45:20,928 --> 00:45:24,349
And they were going on, and on, and on and on… What did Musa(موسى) say?

503
00:45:24,412 --> 00:45:26,370
كَلَّا ۖ إِنَّ مَعِيَ رَبِّي سَيَهْدِينِ

504
00:45:26,394 --> 00:45:30,474
No! Allah is with me and He will guide me, Allah will find a way out for me.

505
00:45:32,596 --> 00:45:36,930
Even though his eyes were telling him otherwise and his ears were telling him otherwise,

506
00:45:36,955 --> 00:45:38,350
his eyes tell him it's impossible.

507
00:45:39,191 --> 00:45:42,551
The sea and the army, his ears are telling him, it's impossible.

508
00:45:42,575 --> 00:45:48,515
Because of all of the whispering of Bannu Israel(بنواسرائيل) but his heart is telling him no!

509
00:45:49,277 --> 00:45:50,953
His heart is telling him believe in Allah.

510
00:45:51,788 --> 00:45:58,825
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ split the sea for Musa(موسى) and destroyed Firaun(فرعون).

511
00:46:03,377 --> 00:46:09,039
Therefore Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will find a way out for you and to apply this on an individual basis

512
00:46:09,064 --> 00:46:14,285
we talked about it on the society level on an individual basis,

513
00:46:14,491 --> 00:46:19,223
if you have Taqwa(تقوى) in Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will provide a way out for you,

514
00:46:20,361 --> 00:46:24,585
in case you get into trouble, or in case you are poor, on in case you are in need,

515
00:46:24,610 --> 00:46:26,353
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will find a way out for you.

516
00:46:27,214 --> 00:46:31,246
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will help you, have that Yaqeen(يقين) in Allah

517
00:46:31,472 --> 00:46:34,586
وَمَن يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَل لَّهُ مَخْرَجًا ۝ وَيَرْزُقْهُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَحْتَسِبُ

518
00:46:34,660 --> 00:46:35,819
Rizq(رزق) will come to you.

519
00:46:38,372 --> 00:46:43,790
Younus عليه السّلام was stuck in the stomach of the whale, under three levels of darkness

520
00:46:44,044 --> 00:46:48,116
 Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ delivered him to safety, because of his Taqwa(تقوى).

521
00:46:56,088 --> 00:47:00,459
Abdullah Bin Zaid Al-Ansari(عبدالله بن زيد ألأنصاري) travelled to Madina

522
00:47:00,541 --> 00:47:02,497
to deliver the news to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

523
00:47:04,073 --> 00:47:09,740
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was delivering Khutba(خطبه) on the Mimber(ممبر), on the pulpit

524
00:47:11,179 --> 00:47:12,835
and he saw Abdullah Bin Zaid(عبدالله بن زيد) coming in.

525
00:47:13,056 --> 00:47:15,210
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was, by the way,

526
00:47:15,266 --> 00:47:20,917
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would be extremely concerned with,

527
00:47:21,079 --> 00:47:24,771
what is happening on the front lines

528
00:47:25,923 --> 00:47:30,540
and he would sometimes be so excited to know the news.

529
00:47:30,565 --> 00:47:36,254
He would go outside of Madina in order to meet the messengers

530
00:47:38,067 --> 00:47:42,938
and he cannot sleep, he would spend his sleepless nights thinking about

531
00:47:42,962 --> 00:47:45,781
what's happening with the Muslims on the front line and it would be making Dua(دُعَا) for them.

532
00:47:46,754 --> 00:47:49,574
So, as soon as this Abdullah Bin Zaid(عبدالله بن زيد) coming in and he is on the Mimber(ممبر)

533
00:47:49,599 --> 00:47:51,166
he said: What's the news?

534
00:47:51,857 --> 00:47:54,055
He cut the Khutba(خطبه) and he said: "What's the news?"

535
00:47:55,372 --> 00:47:58,801
Abdullah Bin Zaid(عبدالله بن زيد) was very wise, he did not answer he said;

536
00:47:58,826 --> 00:48:00,385
أَتَاكَ الّْخَبَرْ يا أمير الّمومنين

537
00:48:00,409 --> 00:48:02,716
News is on its way to you Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين),

538
00:48:04,603 --> 00:48:07,095
until he crossed the lines and he came to Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين)

539
00:48:07,120 --> 00:48:09,468
and he whispered the news into his ears.

540
00:48:10,189 --> 00:48:12,622
He did not want to give the news publicly

541
00:48:13,781 --> 00:48:17,515
until the Khalifah(خليفه) delivers it himself because it's not good news.

542
00:48:19,218 --> 00:48:20,949
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه  said;

543
00:48:20,973 --> 00:48:27,946
أَللَّهُمَّ كُلَّ مُسْلِمٍ فِيْ حِلٍّ مِنِّيْ أَنَا فِئَةْ كُلِّ مُسْلِمٍ

544
00:48:28,524 --> 00:48:32,724
مَنْ لَّقِيَ الّعَدُوْ فَفُظِعَ بِشَيْءٍ مِّنْ أَمْرِهِ فَأَناَ لَه’ فِئَةَ

545
00:48:33,377 --> 00:48:39,330
يَرْحَمُ اللهُ أَبَا عُبَيْد، لَوْ كَانَ إِنْحَازَإِلَيَّ لَكُنْتُ لَه’ فِئَة

546
00:48:40,283 --> 00:48:43,500
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I am the Fea(فِئَةَ) of every Muslim.

547
00:48:44,026 --> 00:48:45,502
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says in Qur'an;

548
00:48:47,884 --> 00:48:57,466
إِلَّا مُتَحَرِّفًا لِّقِتَالٍ أَوْ مُتَحَيِّزًا إِلَىٰ فِئَةٍۢ

549
00:48:59,886 --> 00:49:02,890
You are not allowed to retreat from the battle.

550
00:49:03,714 --> 00:49:11,580
وَمَن يُوَلِّهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍۢ دُبُرَهُۥٓ إِلَّا مُتَحَرِّفًا لِّقِتَالٍ أَوْ مُتَحَيِّزًا إِلَىٰ فِئَةٍۢ فَقَدْ بَآءَ بِغَضَبٍۢ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ

551
00:49:12,404 --> 00:49:15,466
You are not allowed to retreat from the battle.

552
00:49:15,491 --> 00:49:19,302
And we know that retreating from the battle is one of the seven major sins.

553
00:49:19,708 --> 00:49:23,785
You are not allowed to retreat from the battle except in two situations.

554
00:49:23,809 --> 00:49:29,980
Number one, you are making a tactical retreat in order to attack again

555
00:49:30,414 --> 00:49:36,868
or Number two, you are retreating to join with another Muslim force or group.

556
00:49:38,317 --> 00:49:43,927
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I am that force for every Muslim.

557
00:49:44,497 --> 00:49:49,921
May Allah have mercy on Abu Obaid(أبوعبيد)! Why didn't he come back to me?

558
00:49:50,728 --> 00:49:53,203
Why did he have to carry on fighting?

559
00:49:54,228 --> 00:49:59,343
Why didn't he come back to me and I would be the force in which he could fall back on,

560
00:49:59,973 --> 00:50:04,730
and I would give him reinforcements to go back and fight.

561
00:50:05,637 --> 00:50:11,492
See, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was thinking about it from the approach of the leader,

562
00:50:12,098 --> 00:50:14,993
Abu Obaid(أبوعبيد) might have been thinking about it from another approach.

563
00:50:17,807 --> 00:50:21,932
There are two options dying as a shaheed or victory.

564
00:50:22,650 --> 00:50:23,967
إِمَّاالّقَتْلَ وَإِمَّا الشَّهَادَةْ

565
00:50:24,267 --> 00:50:25,231
And these are called.

566
00:50:25,708 --> 00:50:26,788
"إِهْدَالّحُسْنَيَيْنَ"

567
00:50:27,729 --> 00:50:33,862
The two goods, the two virtues, one is dying as a shaheed(شهيد)

568
00:50:33,887 --> 00:50:35,960
and the other one is being victorious.

569
00:50:37,581 --> 00:50:42,127
From a strictly reward point of view

570
00:50:42,276 --> 00:50:45,116
it is more rewarding to die as the shaheed(شهيد) than it is to win.

571
00:50:46,503 --> 00:50:50,527
Therefore on an individual basis the Sahabah(صحابه) would want to die

572
00:50:51,184 --> 00:50:52,856
because it carries more Ajr(أجْر).

573
00:50:54,092 --> 00:50:57,674
However, the leader Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) since he is the Khalifah(خليفه)

574
00:50:58,717 --> 00:51:05,509
he is more concerned with having Islam spread, being victorious, winning.

575
00:51:06,017 --> 00:51:08,111
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was very careful

576
00:51:09,416 --> 00:51:13,340
and he did not want the Muslims to fall into destruction and perish.

577
00:51:16,359 --> 00:51:18,040
And that was the concern of the Khulafaa(خلفاء).

578
00:51:18,132 --> 00:51:22,755
Umar Bin Abdel Aziz رضي الله عنه, the first thing he did as soon as it became Khalifah(خليفه).

579
00:51:23,242 --> 00:51:29,204
He gave orders to have the army that is laying siege to Constantinople to come back.

580
00:51:29,872 --> 00:51:36,340
Why? Because that army was suffering the cold weather and hunger and they were dying.

581
00:51:37,391 --> 00:51:41,699
The only reason why the previous Khalifah(خليفه) had them there, is out of stubbornness.

582
00:51:42,064 --> 00:51:44,147
He wanted Constantinople to fall.

583
00:51:45,719 --> 00:51:48,837
And even though he was receiving news that the Muslims were dying

584
00:51:48,862 --> 00:51:50,921
because of hunger, disease and cold weather.

585
00:51:51,237 --> 00:51:54,831
He had the army carry on laying that siege.

586
00:51:55,292 --> 00:51:58,128
Umar Bin Abdel Aziz(عمربن عبدالعزيز) immediately, called the Muslims back.

587
00:52:01,134 --> 00:52:04,566
Even though everyone who was dying, was dying as a Shaheed(شهيد).

588
00:52:10,646 --> 00:52:14,569
Al-Musanna Bin Harisa Ash-Shaibani(ألمثنى بن حارثه ألشيباني) is now the leader again.

589
00:52:15,412 --> 00:52:19,490
He has assume leadership in many different battles

590
00:52:19,515 --> 00:52:22,523
he was also the leader in the time of Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه.

591
00:52:22,649 --> 00:52:25,734
So, now he became the leader he asked for reinforcements.

592
00:52:25,759 --> 00:52:28,559
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) sent him some reinforcements.

593
00:52:30,261 --> 00:52:33,828
Same thing happens because Iraq is the land of rivers.

594
00:52:34,846 --> 00:52:42,102
He was on the river and the enemy was across him.

595
00:52:42,526 --> 00:52:46,059
And they said: Do you want to cross over to us or shall we cross over to you.

596
00:52:46,084 --> 00:52:48,308
He said: "No you cross over to us".

597
00:52:49,157 --> 00:52:51,483
We are not crossing over to you, you come to us.

598
00:52:56,562 --> 00:53:04,227
They  cross over, Al-Musanna(ألمثنى) gives his instructions to the Muslims,

599
00:53:06,168 --> 00:53:07,322
you make Takbeer(تكبير),

600
00:53:07,774 --> 00:53:14,216
 first Takbeer(تكبير), second Takbeer(تكبير), third Takbeer(تكبير), fourth Takbeer(تكبير) and then you charge.

601
00:53:15,672 --> 00:53:21,014
But the Persian army did not give them that chance.

602
00:53:21,629 --> 00:53:24,018
they attacked immediately after the first Takbeer(تكبير).

603
00:53:26,804 --> 00:53:31,989
Al-Musanna(مثنى) has told his army previously, this was Ramadan(رمضان).

604
00:53:32,452 --> 00:53:36,860
He said: You are fasting and fasting weakens your body.

605
00:53:38,350 --> 00:53:40,671
My advice is that you break your fast.

606
00:53:42,399 --> 00:53:48,027
They followed his advice, and they broke their fast.

607
00:53:48,876 --> 00:53:53,179
He told them, that food will strengthen you.

608
00:53:53,535 --> 00:53:57,310
So, they had their meal middle of the day, even though this was Ramadan(رمضان).

609
00:53:59,801 --> 00:54:06,476
So, they are allowed to break their fast if, it is Harb(حرب), if it is war

610
00:54:06,811 --> 00:54:11,461
that is established in the Shariah(شريعة), because at that particular moment,

611
00:54:12,061 --> 00:54:15,051
the fighting is more virtuous than the fasting.

612
00:54:16,087 --> 00:54:18,869
So, it takes precedence over fasting,

613
00:54:20,172 --> 00:54:26,145
and even if somebody wants to combine between fighting and fasting,

614
00:54:26,629 --> 00:54:30,981
it is better that they don't, because fasting weakens you.

615
00:54:31,349 --> 00:54:34,547
And you need to have all of the stamina and strength that you can.

616
00:54:35,559 --> 00:54:37,187
So, he had them break their fasting.

617
00:54:37,801 --> 00:54:40,791
Also in this particular Battle of Boweb(ألبُوَيب).

618
00:54:40,815 --> 00:54:43,031
After the Muslims won, they won this battle.

619
00:54:43,942 --> 00:54:49,137
Al-Muthanna(مثنى) sent food to the women's camp.

620
00:54:50,091 --> 00:54:53,003
These are the families that accompany their husbands.

621
00:54:53,845 --> 00:54:58,575
So, they were not close to the battle ground there were far away to keep them safe,

622
00:55:00,488 --> 00:55:07,726
Al-Musanna(مثنى) he sent a Christian man to take that food to the woman.

623
00:55:08,920 --> 00:55:13,611
He's an Arab Christian and he had a group of men with him and they're taking the food

624
00:55:14,482 --> 00:55:19,412
to the women and children when the women saw them coming,

625
00:55:19,437 --> 00:55:21,636
they didn't know who they were.

626
00:55:22,244 --> 00:55:26,377
 So, they all armed themselves with poles

627
00:55:27,037 --> 00:55:32,866
and sticks and went out to fight, when this man saw that,

628
00:55:32,905 --> 00:55:35,384
he said: "This is how women should be"

629
00:55:36,558 --> 00:55:38,804
and then he gave them the news of victory.

630
00:55:39,130 --> 00:55:42,385
He said: I am here just to give you this food and not here to fight,

631
00:55:43,997 --> 00:55:48,291
but this shows us that the woman in those days were strong

632
00:55:49,624 --> 00:55:52,824
and they were stronger than the men today.

633
00:55:56,390 --> 00:56:02,965
The Sahabiaat(صحابيات) and Tabiaat(تابيعات) would be willing to fight, if they had to,

634
00:56:04,137 --> 00:56:09,456
not only if they had to but some of them volunteered in fighting like Nusaiba Bint Ka'abرضي الله عنها,

635
00:56:09,503 --> 00:56:11,748
 and some of the other Ansaar(أنْصَار),

636
00:56:11,836 --> 00:56:14,484
Ansaariaat(أنصاريات) especially the woman of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) were strong,

637
00:56:16,118 --> 00:56:18,722
don't you remember the what Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

638
00:56:19,344 --> 00:56:22,659
We used to have the upper hand over our women in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) in Makkah.

639
00:56:22,950 --> 00:56:27,197
And we come here and we find women, who had the upper hand over their husbands.

640
00:56:27,864 --> 00:56:32,909
So, the women of Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) were strong, not only at their homes,

641
00:56:32,995 --> 00:56:34,562
but also in the battlefield.

642
00:56:35,031 --> 00:56:40,191
Nusaiba Bint Ka'ab(نُصيبه بنت كعب) was involved in fighting

643
00:56:40,960 --> 00:56:45,115
and she said: I had 12 injuries in my body on the day of Yarmook(يرموك),

644
00:56:46,830 --> 00:56:53,876
Khalid Bin Waleed رضي الله عنه sent me a physician to take care of me

645
00:56:54,551 --> 00:56:57,484
because he was a man who took great care of us.

646
00:56:59,051 --> 00:57:05,730
And then she said, she had 12 injuries in her body.

647
00:57:05,755 --> 00:57:09,201
And the way they would heal those injuries in those days is,

648
00:57:09,436 --> 00:57:10,434
what would they do?

649
00:57:10,622 --> 00:57:15,533
Would they bring any anti bacteria, medicine and antibiotics.

650
00:57:17,790 --> 00:57:21,873
What they would do, is they would pour over the injury, boiling oil,

651
00:57:23,236 --> 00:57:25,658
they would pour over the injury, boiling oil.

652
00:57:26,190 --> 00:57:28,657
What that does is, it kills the germs.

653
00:57:29,174 --> 00:57:36,316
So, it prevents infections and it also stops the bleeding

654
00:57:37,310 --> 00:57:43,969
and it burns the surface of the injury and that helps the healing.

655
00:57:45,065 --> 00:57:46,134
So, it seals it.

656
00:57:46,358 --> 00:57:51,012
It burnt, it sealed, no infections can get in.

657
00:57:52,079 --> 00:57:58,094
She said, that the healing process was more painful than the injuries themselves.

658
00:58:01,941 --> 00:58:04,050
So, this tells you that these were very strong women,

659
00:58:04,527 --> 00:58:12,016
these were very strong women, for her to have patience to endure all of that pain - voluntarily.

660
00:58:12,072 --> 00:58:16,526
I mean, she chose to go into it and because it's not fardh(فرض) on them.

661
00:58:17,412 --> 00:58:21,686
She chose to, it tells you something about their love of Allah

662
00:58:23,385 --> 00:58:27,459
because remember, in those days there was no anesthesia.

663
00:58:34,647 --> 00:58:42,572
The next battle or series of raids really, commanded by Al-Musanna Bin Harisa Ash-Shaibani(ألمثنى بن حارثه ألشيباني)

664
00:58:43,221 --> 00:58:47,337
were against economical targets of the enemy.

665
00:58:48,550 --> 00:58:51,948
He attacked their markets,

666
00:58:52,782 --> 00:58:58,842
they had these markets, where all of the businessmen would come.

667
00:58:59,051 --> 00:59:04,799
It's like a fairground or tradeshow, you'd name it, whatever you want.

668
00:59:04,824 --> 00:59:10,293
So, they would bring all of their items merchandise to this market.

669
00:59:12,553 --> 00:59:17,434
And they would have more than one market, Al-Muthanna(ألمثنى) targeted these markets

670
00:59:17,895 --> 00:59:22,087
and he told his men to take nothing but gold and silver,

671
00:59:23,973 --> 00:59:27,792
you leave the food behind you leave the clothes behind, you just go after the gold and silver.

672
00:59:29,414 --> 00:59:34,551
And you only take other items, you take as much as your camel can carry, don't take more.

673
00:59:35,609 --> 00:59:38,520
But you should devote the effort to targeting the gold and silver.

674
00:59:39,692 --> 00:59:42,425
The reasoning behind that is Al-Musanna Bin Harisa Ash-Shaibani(ألمثنى بن حارثه ألشيباني)

675
00:59:42,981 --> 00:59:49,709
wants to finance his campaigns against the enemy from his enemies own pocket.

676
00:59:51,061 --> 00:59:54,076
Number two, the Muslims were in need.

677
00:59:54,709 --> 00:59:59,752
And Number three, it is to weaken the enemy.

678
01:00:00,853 --> 01:00:05,131
So, it was an economical war against the Persian Empire.

679
01:00:05,690 --> 01:00:09,193
So, they raided these markets and they did it with lightening speed

680
01:00:10,291 --> 01:00:13,107
headed by Al-Musanna Bin Harisa Ash-Shaibani(ألمثنى بن حارثه ألشيباني).

681
01:00:13,580 --> 01:00:17,867
They used the best horses that they had, the Arabian horses very fast

682
01:00:19,043 --> 01:00:23,813
and they're on their way back and it all happened within one day.

683
01:00:24,356 --> 01:00:31,427
And they covered the distance of more than 60 miles, which is quite significant.

684
01:00:31,716 --> 01:00:34,791
Talking about their form of transportation in those days.

685
01:00:34,815 --> 01:00:37,426
You travelled, you attacked, you come back.

686
01:00:38,728 --> 01:00:42,696
On their way back, they heard some noise.

687
01:00:43,520 --> 01:00:49,467
So, one of the soldiers said: This must be an army attacking us.

688
01:00:52,776 --> 01:00:54,964
Al-Musanna Bin Harisa Ash-Shaibani(ألمثنى بن حارثه ألشيباني), he said;

689
01:00:55,421 --> 01:00:58,935
تَنَاجَوْا بِالْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوَى وَلَا تَنَاجَوْ بِالْإ ثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانَ

690
01:00:59,804 --> 01:01:02,813
 Don't speak evil but speak good.

691
01:01:04,818 --> 01:01:08,095
أُنْظُرُوْا فِي الّأُمُوْرِ وَقَدِّرُوْهَاأحسبوها ثُمَّ تَكَلَّمُوْا

692
01:01:08,427 --> 01:01:10,814
 Think about you say before you say it.

693
01:01:12,263 --> 01:01:17,419
Think about it, assess the situation make the right judgment and then speak,

694
01:01:17,559 --> 01:01:18,759
don't speak first.

695
01:01:19,539 --> 01:01:22,564
إِنَّه’ لَمْ يَبْلُغَ ألْتَدَّبِرْمَدِيْنَتَهُمْ بَعْدْ

696
01:01:23,008 --> 01:01:27,072
وَلَوْبَلَغَهُمْ لَحَالَ الرُّعْبَ بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ طَلَبِكُمْ

697
01:01:28,213 --> 01:01:31,849
Their army didn't even received the warning yet.

698
01:01:33,361 --> 01:01:38,352
Not only is the army not following us, they didn't even know about what happened

699
01:01:39,528 --> 01:01:45,849
our attack was so swift and fast the news didn't even reached the army

700
01:01:45,873 --> 01:01:51,187
and then he said: And if it did, fear will prevent them from following you

701
01:01:52,062 --> 01:01:56,284
because these raids throw fear in the hearts of the enemy

702
01:01:56,308 --> 01:02:01,915
and this fear can last for an entire day, these swift ambushes,

703
01:02:02,746 --> 01:02:06,836
they cast fear in the hearts of the enemy as Musanna Bin Harisa(مثنى بن حارثه) said;

704
01:02:07,394 --> 01:02:11,904
It will make them terrified, it would put them in a state of shock for 24 hours,

705
01:02:11,929 --> 01:02:13,309
don't worry they're not going to come.

706
01:02:16,039 --> 01:02:19,738
إِنَّ لِلْغَارَاتِ رَوْعَاتْ تَنْتَشِرُ عَلَيْهَا يَوْمًا إِلَى الَّيْلَ

707
01:02:20,093 --> 01:02:24,818
وَلَوْ أَدْرَكُوْكُمْ لَقَا تَلْنَهُمْ لِاثْنَتَيْنَ، إِلْتَمَاسَ الْأَجْرَ وَرَجَاءًالنَّصَرْ

708
01:02:24,843 --> 01:02:26,632
And if they do come, so What?

709
01:02:27,354 --> 01:02:33,808
We'll fight them for two reasons to get the Ajr(أجْر) the from Allah and to get victory.

710
01:02:35,090 --> 01:02:39,673
إِنَّ خليفة رسول الله أَبَا بَكْر أَوْصَانَا أَنْ نُقَلِّلَ ألْعَرْجِّةْ

711
01:02:39,971 --> 01:02:43,475
وَنُسْرِعَ ألْكَرَّةَّ فِيْ الّغَارَاتَ وَنُسْرِعَ فِيْ غَيْرِ ذَلِكَ

712
01:02:44,224 --> 01:02:50,137
I'm doing this because the Khalifah(خليفه) of Rasool Ullah, Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه told me

713
01:02:50,502 --> 01:02:53,242
 to be very swift and fast in my raids.

714
01:02:54,428 --> 01:03:00,045
This was the advice of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) that he gave to Musanna(مثنى) to be very fast.

715
01:03:00,748 --> 01:03:06,340
It's pretty much similar to what is called today the guerrilla warfare method.

716
01:03:06,827 --> 01:03:16,169
Which is based on small groups attacking swiftly and retreating after ambushing the enemy.

717
01:03:17,536 --> 01:03:19,876
What was the response of the people of Faris.

718
01:03:22,354 --> 01:03:27,220
What happened to them was because of what Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ created among them.

719
01:03:27,245 --> 01:03:29,271
The disunity that Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ created among them.

720
01:03:30,043 --> 01:03:34,711
So, the people are Faris(فارس), Persia came to Rustum(رستم) and Feroze(فيروز) and they said;

721
01:03:35,137 --> 01:03:39,495
أَيْنَ يَذْهَبْ بِكُمُا الْإِخْتِلَافَ حَتَّى وَهَنْتُمَا أَهْلِ فَارِس

722
01:03:40,090 --> 01:03:44,643
This disunity of yours has weakened the people of Persia.

723
01:03:45,407 --> 01:03:49,339
وَأَطْمَاتُمَا فِيْهِمْ عَدُوَّهُمْ

724
01:03:49,608 --> 01:03:54,811
 And you made the enemy greedy in our land.

725
01:03:55,337 --> 01:04:00,016
وَالله مَا جَرَّ هَذَا أَلّوَهَنْ عَلَيْنَا غَيْرَكُمْ يَا مَعْشَرَالْقُوَّادَ

726
01:04:00,728 --> 01:04:07,056
This defeat that we are suffering now is because of you our leaders.

727
01:04:08,027 --> 01:04:11,214
لَقَدْ فَرَّقْتُّمْ بَيْنَ أَهَل لْفَارِس وَثَبَّطّتُمُوْهُمْ عَنْ عَدُوِّهِمْ

728
01:04:12,010 --> 01:04:15,441
مَا بَعْدَ بَغْدَادْ وَسَابَاطْ وَتَكْرِيْتَ إِلَّا الْمَدَائِنْ

729
01:04:15,902 --> 01:04:20,368
What is left after Baghdad(بغداد), Sabaat(سبات) and Tikrit(تكريت) except Al-Madaen(ألمدائن)?

730
01:04:20,686 --> 01:04:23,901
So, they mentioned the names of some of the major towns that fell.

731
01:04:24,357 --> 01:04:29,636
They said: Tikrit(تكريت), Baghdad(بغداد) and Sabaat(سبات) have fell under the Muslims.

732
01:04:30,977 --> 01:04:33,135
All what is left is our capital Al-Madaen(ألمدائن).

733
01:04:33,579 --> 01:04:34,460
 So, they said;

734
01:04:35,009 --> 01:04:40,909
وَالله لَتَجْتَمِعَانْ أَوْلَنَبْدِأَنَّ بِكُمَا قَبْلَ أَنْ يَشْمَتَ بِنَا شَامِتْ

735
01:04:41,628 --> 01:04:46,030
 You either unify our ranks or we're going to kill you first.

736
01:04:47,503 --> 01:04:52,712
وَالله لَوْ لَا أَنَّ فِيْ قَتْلِكُمْ هَلَاكُنَا لَعَجَّلْنَا لَكُمُ الْقَتْلَ السَّاعَة

737
01:04:53,037 --> 01:04:58,517
If it wasn't that killing, you will weaken us further, we would have killed you first.

738
01:04:59,342 --> 01:05:04,080
وَلَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهُوْا لَنُهْلِكَنَّكُمْ ثُمَّ نَهْلَكْ  وَقَدْ أَشْتَفَيْنَا مِنْكُمْ

739
01:05:04,135 --> 01:05:07,193
And if you don't unify now, we will kill you

740
01:05:08,093 --> 01:05:10,018
 even if we're going to end up losing.

741
01:05:10,642 --> 01:05:15,179
So, that when we lose, we would at least have taken revenge from you.

742
01:05:15,604 --> 01:05:17,866
Because this is happening because of you.

743
01:05:19,205 --> 01:05:22,224
These were very serious threats from the people of Persia.

744
01:05:22,668 --> 01:05:27,036
They're waken up to the threat knocking on their doors.

745
01:05:27,200 --> 01:05:30,919
The Muslims were now way into Iraq.

746
01:05:33,227 --> 01:05:35,049
So, what they did is,

747
01:05:36,263 --> 01:05:41,903
 This was a kingdom, it was ruled by Royal Family,

748
01:05:43,046 --> 01:05:46,597
and you had to have royal blood to be the king.

749
01:05:47,765 --> 01:05:51,806
However, one of their earlier kings, what he did was,

750
01:05:52,509 --> 01:05:58,126
he gathered all of his brothers and their sons and he executed them all.

751
01:05:59,353 --> 01:06:04,793
The reason why he did that is he doesn't want anyone to compete with him in the future.

752
01:06:06,493 --> 01:06:10,783
So, He wanted the royal blood to dry out.

753
01:06:11,201 --> 01:06:14,701
So, that he ensures that he will carry on.

754
01:06:16,747 --> 01:06:20,189
What he really did was he shot himself in the foot, he died,

755
01:06:20,747 --> 01:06:22,659
and there was nobody to take over after him.

756
01:06:23,609 --> 01:06:28,661
So, the kingdom was transferred to a woman from the royal family,

757
01:06:30,763 --> 01:06:32,162
and then she was killed.

758
01:06:32,186 --> 01:06:37,874
So, another woman took over, and she was incapable of leading the Empire,

759
01:06:39,465 --> 01:06:42,878
and that is when Rustam(رستم) and Feroze(فيروز) who are not from the royal family

760
01:06:42,903 --> 01:06:44,983
but they are military generals.

761
01:06:45,197 --> 01:06:47,847
They started taking affairs in their own hands.

762
01:06:48,124 --> 01:06:56,135
They didn't claim to be kings, but they were the actual runners of the affairs of Persia.

763
01:06:56,776 --> 01:07:02,327
They were the administrators but since there was no figurehead to lead them.

764
01:07:02,826 --> 01:07:06,479
These two men Feroze(فيروز) and Rustam(رستم) started clashing.

765
01:07:08,226 --> 01:07:09,278
So, what they did,

766
01:07:09,826 --> 01:07:15,326
they gathered all of the women from the royal family of Sassan(ساسان)

767
01:07:16,764 --> 01:07:21,711
and they had them tortured, they were torturing the women from the royal family,

768
01:07:22,172 --> 01:07:27,848
and telling them, trying to extract from them any information.

769
01:07:28,204 --> 01:07:31,379
If there is a surviving male member in the family,

770
01:07:32,274 --> 01:07:34,758
and they were torturing them to get that information.

771
01:07:35,325 --> 01:07:47,379
One of them did in fact claim that there is one man from the royal family,

772
01:07:47,770 --> 01:07:50,436
who is in this faraway area.

773
01:07:51,452 --> 01:07:55,117
And the reason, why he is there is, because his mother feared for his death.

774
01:07:55,850 --> 01:08:02,458
So, she smuggled him away before the king killed all of the male members of the family,

775
01:08:03,351 --> 01:08:06,282
they investigated that story and found it to be true.

776
01:08:07,433 --> 01:08:11,599
So, they called in this young man.

777
01:08:11,707 --> 01:08:14,440
He was 21 years old, his name is Yastajard(يزدجرد)

778
01:08:15,049 --> 01:08:17,940
and they appointed him as Emperor over them.

779
01:08:19,018 --> 01:08:23,606
He was 21 years old, he is Yastajard Al thalith (يزدجردالثالث) the third,

780
01:08:24,172 --> 01:08:29,752
and he now succeeded in unifying the people of the Persian Empire

781
01:08:30,344 --> 01:08:32,371
so now things were different.

782
01:08:33,590 --> 01:08:37,034
Now, the Muslims will be facing a unified foe.

783
01:08:37,983 --> 01:08:42,559
They would be facing the entire Sassaani Empire.

784
01:08:49,886 --> 01:08:54,010
They started mobilizing their forces from the four corners of the Empire,

785
01:08:54,746 --> 01:08:58,114
and news was reaching to Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه

786
01:08:58,707 --> 01:09:06,232
that the Persian Empire is ready to face us with the largest army, they have assembled so far.

787
01:09:07,067 --> 01:09:15,403
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) decided to go out himself and meet the Persian army,

788
01:09:18,069 --> 01:09:21,206
all of the Sahabah(صحابه) agreed to that suggestion

789
01:09:22,162 --> 01:09:24,128
except one Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف).

790
01:09:26,795 --> 01:09:30,407
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) said: If you are killed,

791
01:09:32,368 --> 01:09:36,013
then the Muslims will have no one to go back to,

792
01:09:37,782 --> 01:09:43,181
but why don't you send someone in your place and you stay behind in Madina.

793
01:09:44,103 --> 01:09:50,266
So, if the Muslims lose, then you would be able to lead another campaign against them

794
01:09:51,832 --> 01:09:54,601
and Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) insisted on his opinion,

795
01:09:55,074 --> 01:09:58,445
and he succeeded in convincing, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to stay behind.

796
01:09:58,973 --> 01:10:01,877
But now, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: So, who can I appoint

797
01:10:02,325 --> 01:10:03,987
 for this major battle?

798
01:10:04,926 --> 01:10:11,202
Who is the person who could take care of this major affair?

799
01:10:13,411 --> 01:10:18,981
And he was thinking about it for days, who should I appoint?

800
01:10:19,927 --> 01:10:23,265
 And then one of the Sahabah(صحابه) came to him and said: I found it, I found it,

801
01:10:24,002 --> 01:10:25,092
I found the person.

802
01:10:25,608 --> 01:10:26,786
He said: Who is it?

803
01:10:27,188 --> 01:10:28,804
He said: It's the lion in his den.

804
01:10:28,844 --> 01:10:29,970
He said, Who is it?

805
01:10:30,784 --> 01:10:34,677
The man is getting Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) excited.

806
01:10:34,737 --> 01:10:36,195
He said: It's a lion in his den!

807
01:10:36,235 --> 01:10:37,433
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Who is it?

808
01:10:37,457 --> 01:10:38,486
Who is that lion?

809
01:10:38,931 --> 01:10:40,629
He said: Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد إبن أبي وقاص).

810
01:10:41,737 --> 01:10:43,986
One of the 10 who are given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

811
01:10:45,638 --> 01:10:48,518
A relative of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

812
01:10:49,145 --> 01:10:51,375
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: You have found him.

813
01:10:52,443 --> 01:10:55,054
And he appointed him to lead the army

814
01:10:55,808 --> 01:11:01,333
that would end up fighting one of The most famous battles in our Muslim history.

815
01:11:02,046 --> 01:11:06,475
One of The most important battles ever in the time of Al-Khulafaa(ألْخلفاء).

816
01:11:07,843 --> 01:11:12,393
In fact, it only has one competitor, and that is Ghazwa Al-Yarmook(غزوة اليرموك).

817
01:11:12,913 --> 01:11:15,985
That's the only battle to compete with the importance of this battle.

818
01:11:16,548 --> 01:11:18,151
And what's the name of this battle…?

819
01:11:19,408 --> 01:11:20,336
Al-Qaadsiyaa(ألقادسیة),

820
01:11:21,614 --> 01:11:23,645
Maarikat-Qadisiyyah(معركة القادسية)

821
01:11:31,193 --> 01:11:35,337
This issue was so important Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) overruled

822
01:11:36,412 --> 01:11:45,801
a order that was or a law that was legislated by Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه

823
01:11:46,332 --> 01:11:51,821
and that is that none of the men, who joined in the armies of Ridda(ردة),

824
01:11:52,817 --> 01:11:55,781
against the Muslims should participate in Jihad(جهاد).

825
01:11:57,223 --> 01:11:59,715
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) refused to accept

826
01:11:59,855 --> 01:12:02,965
the former murtaddeen(مرتدين) into the Muslim army.

827
01:12:04,848 --> 01:12:09,852
Many of these murtaddeen(مرتدين) or all of them, the ones that at least survived

828
01:12:10,024 --> 01:12:11,934
all of them, they came back to Islam.

829
01:12:14,595 --> 01:12:18,269
But Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) didn't want them, to join the Muslim army.

830
01:12:18,539 --> 01:12:19,659
 You stay out.

831
01:12:21,808 --> 01:12:24,136
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was so short of men,

832
01:12:25,346 --> 01:12:29,158
he had to recruit the former Murtaddeen(مرتدين).

833
01:12:30,685 --> 01:12:37,399
And now he opened up the gates of recruitment, anyone is welcomed

834
01:12:38,131 --> 01:12:40,022
we need any help that we can get.

835
01:12:41,196 --> 01:12:45,463
So, many of the former Murtaddeen(مرتدين), now they are Muslim they joined in.

836
01:12:48,485 --> 01:12:53,616
Not only that, but Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) when he did not get enough,

837
01:12:54,299 --> 01:12:58,721
when he opened up the doors of recruitment or voluntary,

838
01:12:59,378 --> 01:13:02,787
he didn't received enough soldiers.

839
01:13:03,514 --> 01:13:08,647
He started mandatory military service.

840
01:13:09,450 --> 01:13:15,517
So, the first one to start mandatory military service was Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه.

841
01:13:16,414 --> 01:13:23,279
He sent out letters to the Muslim states saying that any man, who has weapons

842
01:13:23,648 --> 01:13:27,302
and is able to fight must join in the armies.

843
01:13:28,814 --> 01:13:31,329
Why? Because now, we have the major battle of Qaadsiya(قادسية)

844
01:13:31,689 --> 01:13:35,747
and we also have the Roman front which was still going on.

845
01:13:36,301 --> 01:13:40,767
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) needed anyone that could offer help

846
01:13:40,845 --> 01:13:44,654
to step forward and come and join the Armies.

847
01:13:48,557 --> 01:13:52,308
Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه asked Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد بن أبي وقاص)

848
01:13:52,332 --> 01:13:55,711
 to send a delegation to meet with the Persian Emperor.

849
01:13:56,153 --> 01:14:00,449
So, they sent a delegation of 14 men many of them Sahabah(صحابه)

850
01:14:00,866 --> 01:14:03,519
like Mugheerah Bin Shoba(مغيرة بن شعبه), Noman Bin Makran(نعمان بن مقرن) and others,

851
01:14:04,007 --> 01:14:08,791
they went to Yastajard(يزدجرد) and they delivered to him the message from the Khalifah(خليفه).

852
01:14:09,281 --> 01:14:14,396
We are inviting you to Islam, we were people who were misguided

853
01:14:14,420 --> 01:14:17,872
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ guided us through Muhammad ﷺ,

854
01:14:19,345 --> 01:14:23,706
and now we are delivering to you the same invitation that He gave to us.

855
01:14:25,879 --> 01:14:31,547
An-Noman Ibn Makran(نعمان بن مقرن) closed his speech by saying We give you three options.

856
01:14:32,309 --> 01:14:37,419
Number one: You  become Muslim if you do, we would leave you and your land alone.

857
01:14:38,498 --> 01:14:44,994
Number two: If you refuse to become Muslim then we give you the option of paying Jizya(جزية).

858
01:14:46,181 --> 01:14:48,229
If you refused to pay us Jizya(جزية).

859
01:14:48,642 --> 01:14:50,613
Than it is the sword.

860
01:14:52,938 --> 01:14:57,486
Yastajard(يزدجرد) wasn't happy to hear somebody speaking to him like that,

861
01:14:57,646 --> 01:14:59,695
how do you speak to the Emperor in such a way.?

862
01:15:01,005 --> 01:15:03,338
You're not following the protocols.

863
01:15:04,912 --> 01:15:14,089
He said: You were men who were humbled, and never dreamt of attacking our empire.

864
01:15:15,718 --> 01:15:17,033
So, what has happened to you,

865
01:15:17,430 --> 01:15:22,359
if the reason why you are here in our land is beacuse you're hungry, we will feed you.

866
01:15:23,242 --> 01:15:26,398
We will give you back money to go back to your desert.

867
01:15:27,838 --> 01:15:29,589
Noman Bin Makran(نعمان بن مقرن) said;

868
01:15:30,689 --> 01:15:36,211
Number one: You become Muslim if you don't, you pay us Jizya(جزية).

869
01:15:36,907 --> 01:15:38,814
If you don't, then we will fight you.

870
01:15:39,829 --> 01:15:46,636
Yastajard(يزدجرد) said: If it wasn't because messengers are not killed,

871
01:15:46,706 --> 01:15:48,047
I would have killed you all.

872
01:15:48,436 --> 01:15:49,234
Leave!....

873
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:51,349
So, they left.

874
01:15:52,638 --> 01:15:57,291
That was the first delegation that was sent.

875
01:15:58,787 --> 01:16:04,176
Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن أبي وقاص) sent another delegation to the leader of the army which is Rustum(رُستم).

876
01:16:04,244 --> 01:16:08,106
Rustum(رُستم) is now going to lead the battle in Al-Qadsiya(ألقادسية).

877
01:16:09,321 --> 01:16:14,216
Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدإبن أبي وقاص) sent Rab'ee Ibn Amir رضي الله عنه to meet with him.

878
01:16:14,853 --> 01:16:17,920
And that is when an interesting conversation took place.

879
01:16:18,385 --> 01:16:21,490
We'll talk about that In Sha Allah ho Ta'Allah(إن شاء الله تعالى) tomorrow night.

880
01:16:23,270 --> 01:16:26,221
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

881
01:16:30,897 --> 01:16:33,168
You might have time for a question or two?

882
01:16:38,026 --> 01:16:43,222
You mentioned in one of your previous sessions if a Muslim leaves Islam than he should be executed.

883
01:16:43,591 --> 01:16:45,757
Is there any Qur'an Ayah(آية) or it's from Sunnah(سنة)?

884
01:16:45,812 --> 01:16:46,682
It's from Sunnah.

885
01:16:46,777 --> 01:16:48,611
"مَنْ بَدَّلَ دِيْنَه’ فَاقْتُلُوْهْ"

886
01:16:48,808 --> 01:16:51,734
Whoever changes his religion, then execute him.

887
01:16:52,163 --> 01:16:59,795
However, any punishment can only be carried out by the Sultan(سلطان), by the leader.

888
01:17:00,070 --> 01:17:05,025
Law is not taken into individuals hands.

889
01:17:05,928 --> 01:17:09,369
It has to be done through the Muslim government.

890
01:17:12,032 --> 01:17:17,079
You said that Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد إبن أبي وقاص) made Dua(دُعَا) against the man that slandered him,

891
01:17:17,415 --> 01:17:24,330
however we as Muslims should we not make Dua(دُعَا) for them rather than against them?

892
01:17:25,134 --> 01:17:29,171
Which evil against them? Well,

893
01:17:30,092 --> 01:17:39,333
we are allowed to make Dua(دُعَا) against the person if the person oppresses us,

894
01:17:39,872 --> 01:17:49,878
but don’t make Dua(دُعَا) against somebody who, who just hurt you in a very insignificant way.

895
01:17:50,778 --> 01:17:55,168
Don't make Dua(دُعَا) is somebody who is otherwise righteous and good,

896
01:17:55,512 --> 01:17:57,434
just because they made a mistake once.

897
01:17:58,285 --> 01:18:00,039
You make the Dua(دُعَا) against Zalama(ظلماء)

898
01:18:00,996 --> 01:18:04,971
the people to whom oppression is part of their life, the tyrants

899
01:18:04,996 --> 01:18:06,242
you make Dua(دُعَا) against these.

900
01:18:06,745 --> 01:18:09,187
That’s what Musa عليه السّلام did against Firaun(فرعون).

901
01:18:09,821 --> 01:18:19,874
رَبَّنَا اطْمِسْ عَلَىٰ أَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاشْدُدْ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمْ فَلَا يُؤْمِنُوا حَتَّىٰ يَرَوُا الْعَذَابَ الْأَلِيمَ۝

902
01:18:20,683 --> 01:18:26,269
O Allah seal their hearts and destroy their wealth, until they see the punishment from You.

903
01:18:27,159 --> 01:18:29,265
Meaning don't give them a chance to make Toba(توبة).

904
01:18:30,717 --> 01:18:32,582
And Noah عليه السّلام said;

905
01:18:35,386 --> 01:18:38,203
لَا تَذَرْ عَلَى الْأَرْضِ مِنَ الْكَافِرِينَ دَيَّارًا۝

906
01:18:39,105 --> 01:18:43,411
إِنَّكَ إِنْ تَذَرْهُمْ يُضِلُّوا عِبَادَكَ وَلَا يَلِدُوا إِلَّا فَاجِرًا كَفَّارًا۝

907
01:18:43,821 --> 01:18:48,871
O Allah don't leave any disbelieving soul alive on the face of the earth,

908
01:18:49,402 --> 01:18:51,983
he made Dua(دُعَا) against all of the Kafara(كفارا).

909
01:18:53,574 --> 01:18:58,147
Rasool Allah ﷺ made Dua(دُعَا) against Raqal(رقل) and Aquaan(أقعان) and Urana(عرنة),

910
01:18:58,537 --> 01:19:01,416
he made Dua(دُعَا) against some of the Arab tribes who betrayed him.

911
01:19:02,334 --> 01:19:06,599
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه made Dua(دعا) against the People of the Book who are fighting him.

912
01:19:07,224 --> 01:19:10,264
So Dua(دُعَا) against someone is allowed.

913
01:19:11,643 --> 01:19:18,111
But this should not be interpreted to mean that somebody walked next to you

914
01:19:18,136 --> 01:19:19,935
and just hit you and didn't say excuse me.

915
01:19:20,348 --> 01:19:23,316
So, you start, you raise your hands and you make Dua(دُعَا) him.

916
01:19:23,341 --> 01:19:27,495
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY

917
01:19:27,659 --> 01:19:31,827
MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

918
01:19:31,901 --> 01:19:35,923
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW

919
01:19:36,191 --> 01:19:40,421
MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE

